  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "The podcast host Jesse Michels says that in the 1950s the physicist Bryce DeWitt, along with fellow scientists Stanley Deser and Richard Arnowitt, was studying gravity. According to Michels, DeWitt wrote about superconductors, materials that carry electricity with no resistance, and wondered if spinning them could disturb gravity. Michels raises it to suggest that serious work on controlling gravity was going on decades ago, quietly."
